# SD Core for Linux documentation
#
# THE MARKDOWN IS THE SOURCE, same ruling as SD Core for Windows's docs
# (its .gitignore, owner's ruling 26 Aug 2026, questions 15/16), adopted here
# without re-asking per CLAUDE.md's "the linux port should follow the windows
# port decisions where not contraindicated by the differences between the
# two operating systems" - nothing about generated-vs-source docs is
# OS-specific.  The .html and .pdf beside the markdown are generated by the
# tools in tools/, not tracked - a rendered copy would only add a way for
# the two to disagree, and the cost (each PDF ~200KB) makes a one-word fix
# commit a quarter-megabyte of unreadable diff.
*.html
*.pdf
*.zip

# Linux shell/editor litter
*~
.DS_Store

# Python's byte-cache for tools/.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
